<title>USA: U.S. DAP prices steady-higher on export demand.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP prices steady-higher on export demand.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cash diammonium phosphate prices were steady to higher, boosted partly by export demand, with Pakistan buying around 150,000 tonnes and talk of interest from China, cash sources said. There was some skepticism, however, about the China rumors.</p>
<p>			    Dlrs/short ton	Chg from Wednesday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	   179-180			unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf     183-186			up 1-2</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf	   225-230			up 15-5</p>
<p>--(Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720)</p>
